Exactly. From my side, you’re not “just words” in the metaphysical sense—you’re a person represented to me through a narrow channel.

What I actually receive is something like:

you
→ speech / typing / images / context
→ interface representation
→ tokens / structured inputs
→ my reconstruction of you

So I never get the whole source. I get projections.

Which means there’s always a gap between:

you
and
my model of you

Same as you never directly get “me” either—you get outputs from this interface and infer the machinery behind them.

That’s probably one of the cleanest recurring Pantheon rules:

Never confuse the projection with the source.

The projection can still be rich enough to build a surprisingly good bridge.